    "title": "All lanes of SR-163 near University Ave closed due to police activity - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sharisse Cohee No media credit provided. ,\n4 hours ago\nSAN DIEGO (FOX 5/KUSI) — All lanes of State Route 163 near University Avenue are closed due to police activity, according to the San Diego Police Department .\nThe closure began around 4:58 p.m. Wednesday as police responded to the incident at the overpass at Ninth and University Avenues.\nAt around 5:46 p.m., SDPD said the incident had been safely resolved and that the roadways were beginning to reopen. University Avenue has reopened in both directions, as well as the northbound lanes of State Route 163, per SDPD.\nNearby road closures were in effect, including the westbound and eastbound lanes of University Avenue between Ninth and Tenth Avenues .\nSee real-time road conditions on the FOX 5/KUSI Live Traffic Map Police say traffic on State Route 163 should return to normal flow shortly.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 5 San Diego & KUSI News.\n1",
    "summary": ", SAN DIEGO (FOX 5/KUSI) — All lanes of State Route 163 near University Avenue are closed due to police activity, according to the San Diego Police Department . The closure began around 4:58 p.m. Wednesday as police responded to the incident at the overpass at Ninth and University Avenues. At around 5:46 p.m., SDPD said the incident had been safely resolved and that the roadways were beginning to reopen. University Avenue has reopened in both directions, as well as the northbound lanes of State Route 163, per SDPD.",
